xt":"In the ordinary course of business, the Company may provide indemnifications of varying scope and terms to customers, vendors, lessors, business partners and other parties with respect to certain matters, including, but not limited to, losses arising out of the breach of such agreements, services to be provided by the Company or from intellectual property infringement claims made by third parties. The Company may also assume indemnification obligations in strategic transactions, such as its assumption of certain indemnification obligations in its acquisition of RepairPal.","section":"Item 16. Form 10-K Summary.","block":1271,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"b77d4b9fd508d031415bea21e86c3c68cab4247a91f33d01a192320ae9772bef","quote":"On January 17, 2026, the Company and Hargrove Merger Sub, Inc., a wholly owned subsidiary of the Company (“Merger Sub”), entered into an Agreement and Plan of Merger (the “Merger Agreement”) with Hatchify Inc. (“Hatch”) and Fortis Advisors LLC, as the Securityholders’ Representative. Pursuant to the Merger Agreement, on February 2, 2026, Merger Sub merged with and into Hatch, with Hatch continuing as the surviving corporation and a wholly owned subsidiary of the Company (the “Merger”).","context":"Acquisition of Hatchify Inc.","section":"Item 16. Form 10-K Summary.","block":1389,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"d7e830acce402a8b7f5c94dea340eabfbe0a84ff080c7d86757ffe2cdcc10969","quote":"The Company acquired Hatch, an artificial intelligence (“AI”) lead management platform, to further compliment the Company’s AI capabilities and strategy. The initial accounting for this acquisition is incomplete due to the timing of available information and purchase accounting information is still being compiled and is not available for disclosure. The results of operations of the acquired business will be included in the Company’s consolidated results beginning from the date of acquisition.","context":"The Company funded its acquisition of Hatch in part with borrowings under the credit facility. See Note 12, “Commitments and Contingencies,” for additional details. The Company funded the remainder of the purchase price with proceeds from the sale of approximately $162 million of marketable securities subsequent to year end.","section":"Item 16. Form 10-K Summary.","block":1392,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":0},"riskFactors":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"54da8f74d44ca5a870ac9ea3859e659cc60acc67185e7e9c60d8cd162bc29ff4","quote":"Adverse macroeconomic conditions — particularly those affecting local economies — have had, and may continue to have, a significant adverse impact on our business and results of operations, and also exposes our business to other risks.","context":"Risks Related to Our Business and Industry","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":314,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"51e3910afd3a2f57e081b70826383d945f0c27b83b56c0df20be0a54dc915089","quote":"Our business relies on local economies and the consumer spending that drives them, which may be affected by conditions beyond our control, such as unemployment, inflation, interest rate changes, taxes, access to credit, public health issues, natural disasters and adverse weather conditions, among many others. Currently, many businesses in the United States continue to face challenging operating environments amid widespread economic uncertainties, including labor shortages, supply chain issues, inflation and recessionary concerns, and higher interest rates, which have been exacerbated by changes to U.S. tariff policy and immigration enforcement priorities. These challenging macroeconomic conditions have had, and we expect them to continue to have, a significant adverse impact on our business and results of operations.","context":"Adverse macroeconomic conditions — particularly those affecting local economies — have had, and may continue to have, a significant adverse impact on our business and results of operations, and also exposes our business to other risks.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":315,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"3ef10c471ede83267288f48e819f59f60b42d7290e2f9506485b8373d4b2d54b","quote":"For example, adverse macroeconomic conditions have had, and may continue to have, a negative impact on the ability and willingness of advertisers to spend on our products and services. Businesses in our Restaurants, Retail & Other (“RR&O”) categories in particular have faced protracted adverse conditions, which have negatively impacted their advertising spending with us. The weakness we observed in advertiser demand from RR&O businesses beginning in late December 2023 continued throughout 2025, resulting in advertising revenue from RR&O businesses decreasing 6% and paying advertising locations decreasing 3% year over year in 2025. We believe the performance of our RR&O categories in 2025 was primarily due to the challenging operating environment businesses in these categories continue to face, and we expect these challenges to persist and have an adverse impact on our results of operations in 2026.","context":"Our business relies on local economies and the consumer spending that drives them, which may be affected by conditions beyond our control, such as unemployment, inflation, interest rate changes, taxes, access to credit, public health issues, natural disasters and adverse weather conditions, among many others. Currently, many businesses in the United States continue to face challenging operating environments amid widespread economic uncertainties, including labor shortages, supply chain issues, inflation and recessionary concerns, and higher interest rates, which have been exacerbated by changes to U.S. tariff policy and immigration enforcement priorities. These challenging macroeconomic conditions have had, and we expect them to continue to have, a significant adverse impact on our business and results of operations.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":316,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"f0e9c47a6804327b452a3866f593a2b43bcaa7bc9fde76ddc8a0beb89a67c0fc","quote":"Changes in consumer behavior due to adverse economic conditions have also had, and may continue to have, both direct and indirect negative impacts on our business. Conditions that negatively impact consumer spending in local economies impact our business directly through reduced consumer traffic to our platform. For example, we believe economic uncertainties and inflationary pressures contributed to the lack of growth in consumer traffic to our platform in 2025. Because traffic to and user engagement on our platform together impact the number of ads we are able to show as well as the value of those ads to businesses, such negative impacts on consumer activity may also make it more difficult to convince existing and prospective advertisers that our products offer them a material benefit and generate a competitive return relative to other alternatives.","context":"For example, adverse macroeconomic conditions have had, and may continue to have, a negative impact on the ability and willingness of advertisers to spend on our products and services. Businesses in our Restaurants, Retail & Other (“RR&O”) categories in particular have faced protracted adverse conditions, which have negatively impacted their advertising spending with us. The weakness we observed in advertiser demand from RR&O businesses beginning in late December 2023 continued throughout 2025, resulting in advertising revenue from RR&O businesses decreasing 6% and paying advertising locations decreasing 3% year over year in 2025. We believe the performance of our RR&O categories in 2025 was primarily due to the challenging operating environment businesses in these categories continue to face, and we expect these challenges to persist and have an adverse impact on our results of operations in 2026.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":317,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"22b83c3875d0cea1c470e128bb8033657916debfe1327956cdef6e9e76b6da1d","quote":"Conditions that negatively impact consumer spending in local economies also impact our business indirectly as consumers reduce their spending in local economies, compounding challenges for local businesses and further negatively impacting their willingness to spend on our products and services. For example, as adverse conditions in local economies persisted through 2025, they increasingly impacted our Services categories as consumers forwent, delayed or scaled down services projects; as a result, demand from Services businesses for our products and services was more muted than typical through the third quarter and decreased sequentially in the fourth quarter.","context":"Changes in consumer behavior due to adverse economic conditions have also had, and may continue to have, both direct and indirect negative impacts on our business. Conditions that negatively impact consumer spending in local economies impact our business directly through reduced consumer traffic to our platform. For example, we believe economic uncertainties and inflationary pressures contributed to the lack of growth in consumer traffic to our platform in 2025. Because traffic to and user engagement on our platform together impact the number of ads we are able to show as well as the value of those ads to businesses, such negative impacts on consumer activity may also make it more difficult to convince existing and prospective advertisers that our products offer them a material benefit and generate a competitive return relative to other alternatives.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":318,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"9beaa0558ee8f7f0196d732a1ae700dc72b6cf08f169c4162fa42a5c32a7e858","quote":"As macroeconomic uncertainties continue, our business is exposed to a variety of risks, including:","context":"Conditions that negatively impact consumer spending in local economies also impact our business indirectly as consumers reduce their spending in local economies, compounding challenges for local businesses and further negatively impacting their willingness to spend on our products and services. For example, as adverse conditions in local economies persisted through 2025, they increasingly impacted our Services categories as consumers forwent, delayed or scaled down services projects; as a result, demand from Services businesses for our products and services was more muted than typical through the third quarter and decreased sequentially in the fourth quarter.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":319,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"d10ef7881cfd68fb42000f4b571b324dbe3b81897646686547136d519847a143","quote":"•continued reduced demand for our products, lower retention rates, and increased challenges in or cost of acquiring new customers;","context":"As macroeconomic uncertainties continue, our business is exposed to a variety of risks, including:","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":320,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"05c1a011cc7a4bad0baf304d6e3f15be8629c9cc9dbf5e3c2a3bdd251c299ba8","quote":"•reductions in cash flows from operations and liquidity, which impacts our capital allocation strategy in turn;","context":"•continued reduced demand for our products, lower retention rates, and increased challenges in or cost of acquiring new customers;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":321,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"0946caf175373bd4c5d85b1d37ff75cd484bb184f7903aecb28086dfb37d4fa6","quote":"•setbacks on the progress of our strategic initiatives as we reallocate resources to responding to such adverse conditions;","context":"•reductions in cash flows from operations and liquidity, which impacts our capital allocation strategy in turn;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":322,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"f8ce4da7aee302908e7544a088bcd9020f69dcf392b0bf39836d73994eaedbc0","quote":"•reductions in traffic, engagement, and the quantity and quality of the content provided by our users, which may further harm traffic to our platform;","context":"•setbacks on the progress of our strategic initiatives as we reallocate resources to responding to such adverse conditions;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":323,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"051760de427a877381e2674206ba21676609de5df73af26ccb2089db9ab0f918","quote":"•increased fluctuation in our operating results and volatility and uncertainty in our financial projections;","context":"•reductions in traffic, engagement, and the quantity and quality of the content provided by our users, which may further harm traffic to our platform;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":324,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"ef8c97f23690e9af49d305377ee47c1c57e5ca2f73eea3cd1d085c9ea63f0a2f","quote":"•inefficiencies, delays and disruptions in our business due to the illness of key employees or a significant portion of our workforce;","context":"•increased fluctuation in our operating results and volatility and uncertainty in our financial projections;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":325,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"f74ff905070f142ef85e8c0138650671549408d69b37b90faf85ed48ffbee557","quote":"•additional restructuring and impairment charges; and","context":"•inefficiencies, delays and disruptions in our business due to the illness of key employees or a significant portion of our workforce;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":326,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"bcf2a465c3dd1aa3edd7b81c08f2ea551d314c374c9ad0acadf3c34def5af81d","quote":"•operational difficulties due to adverse effects of such conditions on our third-party service providers and strategic partners.","context":"•additional restructuring and impairment charges; and","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":327,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"838fcb2fcbc9afd9d412fb5f9dd385e662ce7fb084cbc1ccbda920c94ef54cf2","quote":"It is not possible for us to predict the remaining duration of the current adverse economic conditions facing local economies, or the duration or magnitude of the resulting adverse impact on our business. We expect that our business will continue to be significantly adversely affected for the duration of any recessionary period or protracted economic downturn. Any prolonged","context":"•operational difficulties due to adverse effects of such conditions on our third-party service providers and strategic partners.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":328,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"5ee9dffe4085a7c203641f8d8293194cf1f631f4e461e2fb43fe5aa170d80d28","quote":"adverse macroeconomic conditions may also fundamentally shift consumer demand or preferences in ways that harm our business, such as consumers’ preference for food delivery over dine-in restaurant experiences following the COVID-19 pandemic, which we believe may be contributing to the weak RR&O traffic we have seen since the pandemic.","context":"Table of Contents","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":331,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"c198270a862776511a2b1cc594a13a201794d6b26ff7a43b41d3aaa239465e2c","quote":"We generate substantially all of our revenue from advertising. If we fail to maintain and expand our base of advertisers, our revenue and our business will be harmed.","context":"adverse macroeconomic conditions may also fundamentally shift consumer demand or preferences in ways that harm our business, such as consumers’ preference for food delivery over dine-in restaurant experiences following the COVID-19 pandemic, which we believe may be contributing to the weak RR&O traffic we have seen since the pandemic.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":332,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"28ec2805c65d949a8ed412ad43a2f4f4d3f73c18a527e22fc9dfcc411bc2acd7","quote":"In order to maintain and expand our advertiser base, we must convince existing and prospective advertisers alike that our advertising products offer them a material benefit and generate a competitive return relative to other alternatives. Adverse macroeconomic conditions may make this more difficult, particularly when such macroeconomic conditions disproportionately affect the local economies, including SMBs, on which we rely, as was the case with the economic impact of the COVID-19 pandemic. Many businesses continue to face supply chain issues, inflation, inventory and labor shortages, and an increased cost of labor, among other challenges. These conditions have had, and we expect them to continue to have, a significant adverse impact on our business and revenue; for example, we believe the challenging operating environment resulting from these macroeconomic pressures has been responsible for the weakness in advertiser demand in our RR&O categories we have been experiencing since late December 2023.","context":"We generate substantially all of our revenue from advertising. If we fail to maintain and expand our base of advertisers, our revenue and our business will be harmed.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":333,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"8ca34b86172be5043a9cce92a6346c55b7680637efdccd3a83f08b19e8a73c4e","quote":"Advertisers will not advertise with us, or they will reduce the prices they are willing to pay to advertise with us, if we do not deliver compelling ad products in an effective manner, or if we do not provide accurate, easy-to-use analytics and measurement solutions that demonstrate the effectiveness and value of our products. As is typical in our industry, our advertisers generally have the ability to cancel their ad campaigns at any time without penalty. If we are unable to quickly and effectively respond to any decrease in customer satisfaction, economic downturn or other change negatively affecting our ability to retain advertisers, our ability to maintain and expand our advertiser base will be harmed.","context":"In order to maintain and expand our advertiser base, we must convince existing and prospective advertisers alike that our advertising products offer them a material benefit and generate a competitive return relative to other alternatives. Adverse macroeconomic conditions may make this more difficult, particularly when such macroeconomic conditions disproportionately affect the local economies, including SMBs, on which we rely, as was the case with the economic impact of the COVID-19 pandemic. Many businesses continue to face supply chain issues, inflation, inventory and labor shortages, and an increased cost of labor, among other challenges. These conditions have had, and we expect them to continue to have, a significant adverse impact on our business and revenue; for example, we believe the challenging operating environment resulting from these macroeconomic pressures has been responsible for the weakness in advertiser demand in our RR&O categories we have been experiencing since late December 2023.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":334,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"7506481fa468af9fc790b6f13abc77a422c62f3a3ac283ea906afc8bfc7aee4c","quote":"In addition, a significant portion of our advertiser base consists of SMBs, which are subject to increased challenges and risks. SMBs often have limited advertising budgets and view online advertising products like ours as experimental and unproven; as a result, we may need to devote additional time and resources to educate them about our products and services. Such businesses have also historically experienced high failure rates, and we must continually add new advertisers to replace those who do not renew their advertising due to factors outside of our control, such as declining advertising budgets, closures and bankruptcies.","context":"Advertisers will not advertise with us, or they will reduce the prices they are willing to pay to advertise with us, if we do not deliver compelling ad products in an effective manner, or if we do not provide accurate, easy-to-use analytics and measurement solutions that demonstrate the effectiveness and value of our products. As is typical in our industry, our advertisers generally have the ability to cancel their ad campaigns at any time without penalty. If we are unable to quickly and effectively respond to any decrease in customer satisfaction, economic downturn or other change negatively affecting our ability to retain advertisers, our ability to maintain and expand our advertiser base will be harmed.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":335,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"ecfd02a0fce626afcef10cf0cbd791a2f41b548fe9a7bee926c74cfb96936cf9","quote":"Our advertising revenue could be impacted by a number of other factors, including, but not limited to:","context":"In addition, a significant portion of our advertiser base consists of SMBs, which are subject to increased challenges and risks. SMBs often have limited advertising budgets and view online advertising products like ours as experimental and unproven; as a result, we may need to devote additional time and resources to educate them about our products and services. Such businesses have also historically experienced high failure rates, and we must continually add new advertisers to replace those who do not renew their advertising due to factors outside of our control, such as declining advertising budgets, closures and bankruptcies.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":336,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"621e84b6516e128bd5a908834d40b5bbe073398eff3ab0a23b93c6eda0bcec6b","quote":"•the perceived effectiveness and acceptance of online advertising generally, particularly among SMBs that may have less experience with it;","context":"Our advertising revenue could be impacted by a number of other factors, including, but not limited to:","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":337,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"e71eae5e7c977bf142aae8c1e8f048827ccbc2a62dcf1e0cb7bb8fdaeaaf3178","quote":"•our ability to drive traffic to our platform, which remains below pre-pandemic levels, and increase user engagement, including engagement with the ads displayed on our platform;","context":"•the perceived effectiveness and acceptance of online advertising generally, particularly among SMBs that may have less experience with it;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":338,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"7f8f1b4789137364d3c512cf664bd260a234b39b59859185cf57223012679121","quote":"•challenging macroeconomic conditions or trends that negatively impact consumer demand, such as the current inflationary environment, which we believe began negatively impacting demand from Services advertisers in 2025, and consumers visiting many types of businesses less frequently than prior to the pandemic;","context":"•our ability to drive traffic to our platform, which remains below pre-pandemic levels, and increase user engagement, including engagement with the ads displayed on our platform;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":339,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"2ece7b945752b022e90da535b7de3db9f05cc087d91139924926838c0740759b","quote":"•the effectiveness of our ad targeting technology and tools for advertisers to optimize their campaigns;","context":"•challenging macroeconomic conditions or trends that negatively impact consumer demand, such as the current inflationary environment, which we believe began negatively impacting demand from Services advertisers in 2025, and consumers visiting many types of businesses less frequently than prior to the pandemic;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":340,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"c7451582dfa602e70f261343486860877b28e43f9fd4e0bb61966dd6663abb8a","quote":"•our ability to innovate and introduce enhanced products meeting advertiser expectations;","context":"•the effectiveness of our ad targeting technology and tools for advertisers to optimize their campaigns;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":341,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"9ac61edbc83ceb393222d2b5daa08c323040af86b81edf294e189284d93749b8","quote":"•product changes or inventory management decisions we may make that change the size, format, frequency or relative prominence of ads displayed on our platform;","context":"•our ability to innovate and introduce enhanced products meeting advertiser expectations;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":342,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"0304faea06e6dcefdb4dce97369a6cd43cbe4a3304219a7dc57963863faf00ff","quote":"•the widespread adoption of any technologies that make it more difficult for us to deliver ads, such as ad-blocking programs;","context":"•product changes or inventory management decisions we may make that change the size, format, frequency or relative prominence of ads displayed on our platform;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":343,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"7d6aae2633812260783e3513953d3204329ad7e39d4671e625585b053e63d25e","quote":"•loss of advertising business to our competitors, including if competitors offer lower priced or more integrated products;","context":"•the widespread adoption of any technologies that make it more difficult for us to deliver ads, such as ad-blocking programs;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":344,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"ab9d5832c336c9586263a400cae82d92f69840279d513622c86c05c8ede6c7e8","quote":"•the prevalence of low-quality or invalid traffic on our platform, such as robots and spiders, which we have discovered in the past and expect to discover in the future, and our ability to detect and prevent click fraud or other invalid clicks on ads;","context":"•loss of advertising business to our competitors, including if competitors offer lower priced or more integrated products;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":345,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"9ac159ce596b472048fd964dd3eb9f567f2671c34de921bd7d9ef1829e1c474b","quote":"•our reputation and perceptions regarding our platform, including of the ratings and reviews that businesses receive from our users — favorable ratings and reviews could be perceived as obviating the need to advertise, while unfavorable ratings and reviews could discourage businesses from advertising to an audience that they perceive as hostile;","context":"•the prevalence of low-quality or invalid traffic on our platform, such as robots and spiders, which we have discovered in the past and expect to discover in the future, and our ability to detect and prevent click fraud or other invalid clicks on ads;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":346,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"8edfdae531c3f48b293bc32a18cefef6d222436c3945af09e5b7b5a2e3e149e0","quote":"•the size and productivity of our sales force, which may be affected by a range of factors, not all of which are within our control;","context":"•our reputation and perceptions regarding our platform, including of the ratings and reviews that businesses receive from our users — favorable ratings and reviews could be perceived as obviating the need to advertise, while unfavorable ratings and reviews could discourage businesses from advertising to an audience that they perceive as hostile;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":347,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"2c706612b89dd17b9e77d0a60280efaca8a030c8ccd51ce26049d16325c86c3f","quote":"•the degree to which businesses choose to reach users through our free products in lieu of our paid products and services; and","context":"Table of Contents","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":350,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"6744558b16faa07f467cd56ecbe97174eed1d1cae171f0eb21b09c55de3155a1","quote":"•the pricing of our products, including the CPCs determined by our auction system, which have increased in recent quarters even as we have delivered fewer ad clicks.","context":"•the degree to which businesses choose to reach users through our free products in lieu of our paid products and services; and","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":351,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"3fdf4e2222d9d2cddd5994f6790444d969317c7c8ac7db7e95faacc05b0d0924","quote":"Any of these or other factors could result in a reduction in demand for our products, which would negatively affect our revenue and operating results.","context":"•the pricing of our products, including the CPCs determined by our auction system, which have increased in recent quarters even as we have delivered fewer ad clicks.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":352,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"41d98b3e41943522347b6e039826bd85a8db0071fffa6f0940d7454b6b061dc2","quote":"Our strategy to grow our business may not be successful and may expose us to additional risks.","context":"Any of these or other factors could result in a reduction in demand for our products, which would negatively affect our revenue and operating results.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":353,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"3506f85afaa021e730048b80b8cfc654f6d81de3909754e947537af74ea34aa8","quote":"Our growth strategy includes priorities such as reconceiving Yelp around answers and actions, delivering AI tools that help service pros and other local businesses grow, operate and succeed, and extending our reach to power local delivery across the AI ecosystem. These initiatives will require substantial investments, involve significant risks and executing on them may prove more difficult than we currently anticipate. We may not succeed in realizing the benefits of these efforts, including growing our revenue and improving our margins, within the time frame we expect or at all. Even if these initiatives ultimately drive revenue growth, it will likely trail the increase in expenses resulting from our investments.","context":"Our strategy to grow our business may not be successful and may expose us to additional risks.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":354,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"ae12496d16e5870184e7997ae6685749e855047c4c70d9b663f9852ae8fcfdc4","quote":"Our ability to execute each of our strategic priorities depends on our ability to develop innovative, relevant and useful products in a timely manner. Developing successful products requires substantial investments, and such investments may not prioritize short-term financial results and may involve significant risks and uncertainties. For example, new products may fail to generate sufficient revenue, operating margin or other value to justify the investments we made in them. This is a particular risk for new products that are unproven or that are outside of our historical core business, including the product roadmap underlying our 2026 strategic initiatives, which aims to deliver innovative AI-powered products and features. Although we have significant experience with AI technologies, the use of, as well as consumer expectations for, such technologies are rapidly evolving and we cannot guarantee that our AI-based products will prove popular with consumers or businesses. Our plans to leverage AI in our product initiatives and business operations also pose particular risks to our business, as further described below.","context":"Our growth strategy includes priorities such as reconceiving Yelp around answers and actions, delivering AI tools that help service pros and other local businesses grow, operate and succeed, and extending our reach to power local delivery across the AI ecosystem. These initiatives will require substantial investments, involve significant risks and executing on them may prove more difficult than we currently anticipate. We may not succeed in realizing the benefits of these efforts, including growing our revenue and improving our margins, within the time frame we expect or at all. Even if these initiatives ultimately drive revenue growth, it will likely trail the increase in expenses resulting from our investments.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":355,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"9d6b0cbd054549c5603a5796f804a05adb38db63c16848389cd61e9b2c327ff6","quote":"Certain of our past strategic decisions may also continue to impact our opportunities and long-term prospects. For example, although our strategic focus on Services businesses in recent years has driven our business performance, our Services business faces industry challenges. In addition to being a highly competitive, fragmented market, it has not yet fully embraced online solutions of the type we offer. Many consumers continue to search for, select and hire service professionals offline through word-of-mouth and referrals. Changing traditional habits is difficult, and the speed and ultimate outcome of the shift of these markets online for consumers and businesses alike is uncertain and may not occur as quickly as we expect, or at all.","context":"Our ability to execute each of our strategic priorities depends on our ability to develop innovative, relevant and useful products in a timely manner. Developing successful products requires substantial investments, and such investments may not prioritize short-term financial results and may involve significant risks and uncertainties. For example, new products may fail to generate sufficient revenue, operating margin or other value to justify the investments we made in them. This is a particular risk for new products that are unproven or that are outside of our historical core business, including the product roadmap underlying our 2026 strategic initiatives, which aims to deliver innovative AI-powered products and features. Although we have significant experience with AI technologies, the use of, as well as consumer expectations for, such technologies are rapidly evolving and we cannot guarantee that our AI-based products will prove popular with consumers or businesses. Our plans to leverage AI in our product initiatives and business operations also pose particular risks to our business, as further described below.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":356,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"82051439fefb068fa6bae6194d899ccc7470937327e413522c7109c51e5d62ed","quote":"If traffic to or user engagement on our platform declines, our revenue, business and operating results may be harmed.","context":"Certain of our past strategic decisions may also continue to impact our opportunities and long-term prospects. For example, although our strategic focus on Services businesses in recent years has driven our business performance, our Services business faces industry challenges. In addition to being a highly competitive, fragmented market, it has not yet fully embraced online solutions of the type we offer. Many consumers continue to search for, select and hire service professionals offline through word-of-mouth and referrals. Changing traditional habits is difficult, and the speed and ultimate outcome of the shift of these markets online for consumers and businesses alike is uncertain and may not occur as quickly as we expect, or at all.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":357,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"e322579ac3ac90f05ffffac9ed047f636f017baf7e2c93667258c3e26caca182","quote":"We derive a substantial majority of our revenue based on our users’ engagement with the ads that we display. Because traffic to and user engagement on our platform together determine the number of ad clicks we are able to deliver, affect the value of those ads to businesses and support the content creation that drives further traffic, our ability to attract, retain and engage visitors on our platform is critical to our business and financial success.","context":"If traffic to or user engagement on our platform declines, our revenue, business and operating results may be harmed.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":358,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"e7d67aea7fd16a7b5cd9f57e2a8c222c2f869a10652593023ed04a79a4fec831","quote":"We have experienced, and expect to continue to experience, declines in our traffic in certain periods for a variety of reasons. For example, because a substantial majority of our traffic goes to our RR&O categories and RR&O traffic is particularly sensitive to changes in consumer confidence levels, our overall traffic levels generally fluctuate with macroeconomic conditions. We believe that the current uncertain and inflationary economic environment continued to have a negative impact on our RR&O traffic in 2025, offsetting modest growth in Services traffic, resulting in our traffic metrics being down modestly year over year. While we cannot predict the remaining duration of the current uncertain economic conditions or the duration or magnitude of their impact on our traffic, we expect traffic to remain challenged in 2026.","context":"We derive a substantial majority of our revenue based on our users’ engagement with the ads that we display. Because traffic to and user engagement on our platform together determine the number of ad clicks we are able to deliver, affect the value of those ads to businesses and support the content creation that drives further traffic, our ability to attract, retain and engage visitors on our platform is critical to our business and financial success.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":359,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"85ddc32ed52159d2dbf66783c14d23834cf8512f8ae22491809d0307cb4c5dd9","quote":"Other factors that could adversely affect our traffic and user engagement include, but are not limited to:","context":"We have experienced, and expect to continue to experience, declines in our traffic in certain periods for a variety of reasons. For example, because a substantial majority of our traffic goes to our RR&O categories and RR&O traffic is particularly sensitive to changes in consumer confidence levels, our overall traffic levels generally fluctuate with macroeconomic conditions. We believe that the current uncertain and inflationary economic environment continued to have a negative impact on our RR&O traffic in 2025, offsetting modest growth in Services traffic, resulting in our traffic metrics being down modestly year over year. While we cannot predict the remaining duration of the current uncertain economic conditions or the duration or magnitude of their impact on our traffic, we expect traffic to remain challenged in 2026.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":360,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"7dd1c7b783bdc37cccb4d891d043f3ea64b119c179989bd6a714697611017ec3","quote":"•other adverse macroeconomic conditions and their negative impact on consumer spending at local businesses;","context":"•our reliance on Internet search engines;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":362,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"bb94c4b8c45cd73fcdb4dea6babfdf684ed5a4fae99b74457948c2e102a4dc0d","quote":"•if users engage with other products, services or activities as an alternative to our platform;","context":"•other adverse macroeconomic conditions and their negative impact on consumer spending at local businesses;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":363,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"51a88154f3110539fa353b541408a21dd777ca8701b7bbb40576ce34ea57ef6e","quote":"•if consumers use AI-powered features of search engines, such as Google’s AI Overviews and AI Mode, AI chatbots or other AI platforms instead of traditional search engines, as these tools often present their results in a format that de-emphasizes links to our platform;","context":"•if users engage with other products, services or activities as an alternative to our platform;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":364,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"2b8a61f1f752f2b69f5ef709aebe9dd054faa268163280d5fa775c47cdb7ee37","quote":"•if users have difficulty installing, updating or otherwise accessing our platform as a result of actions by us or third parties that we rely on to distribute our products, such as application marketplaces and device manufacturers;","context":"Table of Contents","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":367,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"2c9e7692ad76f803be211183ee4fad01fb98137c2ed9be987b0be4d526b422e8","quote":"•if we fail to introduce new and improved products or features that users find engaging, or we introduce new products or features that do not effectively address consumer needs or otherwise alienate consumers;","context":"•if users have difficulty installing, updating or otherwise accessing our platform as a result of actions by us or third parties that we rely on to distribute our products, such as application marketplaces and device manufacturers;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":368,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"0e5a85393f6102d1cbc6af2714000d874c605b210d53251baa81c9ce927c5b9a","quote":"•the quantity and quality of the content contributed by our users, as well as the perceived distribution of such content across the categories of businesses on our platform;","context":"•if we fail to introduce new and improved products or features that users find engaging, or we introduce new products or features that do not effectively address consumer needs or otherwise alienate consumers;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":369,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"84eaca9e6cae4e27cc89a27963c35217244d9034f9f3c50023a274540e618b57","quote":"•increasing competition in the market for information regarding local businesses;","context":"•the quantity and quality of the content contributed by our users, as well as the perceived distribution of such content across the categories of businesses on our platform;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":370,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"67dea0c885bc1f969645cf926b312eea32b2e18b8f77f5ce5c3b928cd4dfc075","quote":"•our ability to manage and prioritize information to ensure users are presented with content that is relevant and helpful to them, including through the effective operation of our automated recommendation software;","context":"•increasing competition in the market for information regarding local businesses;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":371,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"4771ae9c5dc7b2626de072a95f7d201864d7708a537362cd5b5ed935485f785a","quote":"•technical or other problems that negatively impact the availability and reliability of our platform or otherwise affect the user experience, including as a result of infrastructure performance problems and security breaches;","context":"•our ability to manage and prioritize information to ensure users are presented with content that is relevant and helpful to them, including through the effective operation of our automated recommendation software;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":372,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"e96c14fb2131188648f5f1891b369a5e8ad436825c6ef4518522b583e754a4e3","quote":"•if users believe that their experience is diminished as a result of the decisions we make with respect to the frequency, relevance and prominence of the advertising we display;","context":"•technical or other problems that negatively impact the availability and reliability of our platform or otherwise affect the user experience, including as a result of infrastructure performance problems and security breaches;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":373,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"95244e8ebc253aefc0cc7b11193edd67cf810295109d4b01b61cb444c7aae452","quote":"•the adoption of any laws or regulations that adversely affect the growth, popularity or use of our platform or the Internet in general, such as the repeal of Internet neutrality regulations in the United States;","context":"•if users believe that their experience is diminished as a result of the decisions we make with respect to the frequency, relevance and prominence of the advertising we display;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":374,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"665fa6368eddd54ee426ba469a85507536d61ef473798671902d8d0216c1e45f","quote":"•any actions taken by companies with significant market power in the broadband and Internet marketplace that degrade, disrupt or increase the cost of user access to our products and services; and","context":"•the adoption of any laws or regulations that adversely affect the growth, popularity or use of our platform or the Internet in general, such as the repeal of Internet neutrality regulations in the United States;","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":375,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"82ab9b57cc3b872ce508117156eddf9c2d890f632e9009c99424be07370bb64a","quote":"•if we do not maintain our brand image or our reputation is damaged.","context":"•any actions taken by companies with significant market power in the broadband and Internet marketplace that degrade, disrupt or increase the cost of user access to our products and services; and","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":376,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"5fd2de8225d4f50bc6037e7d0a322014d078c373855bf6cac244d7d64b9b7ebb","quote":"As a result of these dynamics, as well as the maturation of our business and our high penetration rates in most major geographic markets within the United States and Canada, we generally expect our traffic to decrease in certain periods going forward. Should our traffic continue to decline, our business and financial performance will become increasingly dependent on driving user engagement on our platform and with the ads that we display, which we may not do successfully.","context":"•if we do not maintain our brand image or our reputation is damaged.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":377,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"d5ad974dad41bda328db4fe0b8baa2e4fdcca5f6fe4156448d0aab29e4dd6398","quote":"We rely on Internet search engines and application marketplaces to drive traffic to our platform, certain providers of which offer products and services that compete directly with our products. If links to our applications and website are not displayed prominently, traffic to our platform could decline and our business would be adversely affected.","context":"As a result of these dynamics, as well as the maturation of our business and our high penetration rates in most major geographic markets within the United States and Canada, we generally expect our traffic to decrease in certain periods going forward. Should our traffic continue to decline, our business and financial performance will become increasingly dependent on driving user engagement on our platform and with the ads that we display, which we may not do successfully.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":378,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"5240196c023035957b341717162e07293bee50aa0fd1c1a4f06e6572d4bad4db","quote":"We rely heavily on Internet search engines, including primarily Google, to drive traffic to our platform through their unpaid search results and on application marketplaces, such as Apple’s App Store and Google’s Play, to drive downloads of our applications. If they fail to drive sufficient traffic to our platform, we may need to increase our marketing spend to acquire additional traffic. We cannot assure you that the value we ultimately derive from any such additional traffic would exceed the cost of acquisition, and the resulting increase in marketing expense may in turn harm our operating results. For example, despite our 2024 initiative to acquire Services projects through paid search resulting in an increase in projects, more ad clicks and lower average CPCs than in the prior year, these improvements did not drive our desired returns in advertiser retention or ad budget increases.","context":"We rely on Internet search engines and application marketplaces to drive traffic to our platform, certain providers of which offer products and services that compete directly with our products. If links to our applications and website are not displayed prominently, traffic to our platform could decline and our business would be adversely affected.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":379,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"dcb338241e657a45a02ba9776058b7cd7fa897330a526b82a02af222ea0ec996","quote":"The amount of traffic we attract from search engines is due in large part to how and where information from and links to our website are displayed on search engine result pages. The specific links to our platform that are displayed in search engine results also impact the quality, including the value and engagement level, of the traffic we receive from search engines. The display, including rankings and links, of unpaid search results can be affected by a number of factors, many of which are not in our direct control, and may change frequently. Search engines have made changes in the past to their ranking algorithms, methodologies and design layouts that have reduced the prominence of links to our platform and negatively impacted the volume and quality our traffic, and we expect they will continue to make such changes from time to time in the future. For example, search engines such as Google have incorporated AI-generated responses to search queries above their organic search results, which has reduced the prominence of links to our platform and may be having a negative impact on our traffic.","context":"We rely heavily on Internet search engines, including primarily Google, to drive traffic to our platform through their unpaid search results and on application marketplaces, such as Apple’s App Store and Google’s Play, to drive downloads of our applications. If they fail to drive sufficient traffic to our platform, we may need to increase our marketing spend to acquire additional traffic. We cannot assure you that the value we ultimately derive from any such additional traffic would exceed the cost of acquisition, and the resulting increase in marketing expense may in turn harm our operating results. For example, despite our 2024 initiative to acquire Services projects through paid search resulting in an increase in projects, more ad clicks and lower average CPCs than in the prior year, these improvements did not drive our desired returns in advertiser retention or ad budget increases.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":380,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":23},"segmentIntelligence":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"09d6ee9085a24f94f292710584854ec6114d254bece5531cda4b8d29a8ca1e29","quote":"We plan to continue our disciplined expense management as we invest in high-return areas to drive profitable growth. Excluding the recently acquired Hatch team and hires to support their growth, we expect headcount to again remain approximately flat year over year in 2026, reflecting both our commitment to driving leverage in the business through our product-led strategy as well as our teams’ abilities to deliver operational efficiencies using AI. We also continue to expect to reduce stock-based compensation expense to less than 6% of revenue by the end of 2027. To support our ongoing repurchase plans, in February 2026, the Board authorized us to repurchase an additional $500.0 million of shares of our outstanding common stock.","context":"Investing for Growth","section":"Item 1. Business.","block":116,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001345016-26-000019","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-27","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001345016","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1345016/000134501626000019/yelp-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326.bin","sha256":"35a7e8b462c290691f2937cd05285a50de1091656607255bfec66e65f7163326"}},{"id":"56868e9633e8ffbb36808de8a6f10ddee2707b0d2c98e55beb20bb8407280d85","quote":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | Three Months EndedDecember 31, | | % Change | | Year Ended December 31, | | % Change | 2025 | | 2024 | | | 2025 | | 2024 | Services | $ | 231,381 | | | $ | 224,840 | | | 3% | | $ | 947,564 | | | $ | 879,092 | | | 8% Restaurants, Retail & Other | 106,829 | | | 120,798 | | | (12)% | | 443,696 | | | 469,928 | | | (6)% Total Advertising Revenue | $ | 338,210 | | | $ | 345,638 | | | (2)% | | $ | 1,391,260 | | | $ | 1,349,020 | | | 3%","context":"The following table presents our advertising revenue by category for the periods presented (in thousands, except percentages):","section":"Item 7. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations.","block":763,"table":" |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | \n | Three Months EndedDecember 31, |  | % Change |  | Year Ended December 31, |  | % Change\n | 2025 |  | 2024 |  |  | 2025 |  | 2024 